      "writtenOn": "2025-07-18T14:20:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In line with what I\u0027ve just suggested in https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/3649034/comment/7f838e18_c5a9606a/, maybe something like this:\n\n```\n\tif (pkvm_finalise_started) {\n\t\t/*\n\t\t * Rollback pkvm initialization. Also the hypervisor will take care\n\t\t * of clearing the pvmfw memory.\n\t\t */\n\t\tkvm_hypercall1(__PKVM_HC_COMMIT_FINALISE, false);\n\t} else {\n\t\t/*\n\t\t * Some CPUs may be already deprivileged but still have access\n\t\t * to the hypervisor memory, so we can clear the pvmfw memory\n\t\t * as soon as possible, before trying to reprivilege CPUs.\n\t\t */\n\t\tpkvm_firmware_rmem_clear();\n\t}\n\n\t/*\n\t * Reprivilege cpus\n\t */\n\t...\n```\n\n?",
      "revId": "98db7e845c96e1088088c5d6029fd35851e5e020",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1e2916ba_d2f5d468",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/pkvm_host.c",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 1448,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-18T14:41:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After more thought: it doesn\u0027t really make much difference whether to clear pvmfw in pKVM in the __PKVM_HC_COMMIT_FINALISE(false) hypercall, or right after returning from this hypercall. So, to keep it simpler and avoid duplicating pvmfw clearing code in the hypervisor, we can call pkvm_firmware_rmem_clear() here in the host (but before reprivileging CPUs, not after it) in both cases, not just if pkvm_finalise_started is false.",
      "parentUuid": "9b2cd540_fc70f3db",
      "revId": "98db7e845c96e1088088c5d6029fd35851e5e020",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d72a0883_73783e8c",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/pkvm_host.c",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 1448,
      "author": {
        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-13T13:02:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree. Just curious: is there an advantage in clearing fw memory before reprivilege? After `__PKVM_HC_COMMIT_FINALISE(false)` is called, the fw memory is accessible to host and would it make a difference clearing it before or after reprivilege?",
      "parentUuid": "1e2916ba_d2f5d468",
      "revId": "98db7e845c96e1088088c5d6029fd35851e5e020",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "526bb3f8_08f2b452",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/pkvm_host.c",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 1448,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-14T19:08:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Realistically, bugs in the reprivileging code are not unlikely, right? So if something goes wrong during reprivileging and the CPU gets stuck in some undefined state, the pvmfw memory ends up not being cleared. So it seems safer to clear it as soon as we can, before reprivileging?",
      "parentUuid": "d72a0883_73783e8c",
      "revId": "98db7e845c96e1088088c5d6029fd35851e5e020",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "15f26945_435296f8",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/pkvm_host.c",
